    },
    {
      "text": "Barfoed&#39;s&nbsp;test",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Benedict&#39;s test",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Seliwanoff&#39;s Test : This test is used to detect the presence of Ketohexose.<br />Reagent : Resorcinol <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo></math> conc. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCl</mi></math>.<br />Barfoed&#39;s Test : It is&nbsp;used to detect Monosaccharide by reduction of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cu</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>II</mi><mo>)</mo></math> into Copper (I). Fehling Solution: It is used to detect aldehyde by reduction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cu</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>II</mi><mo>)</mo></math> into <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cu</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>)</mo></math>. Biuret&nbsp;Test : Use to detect presence of peptide bond in protein by reduction of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cu</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>II</mi><mo>)</mo></math> into <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cu</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>)</mo></math>."
  }
